1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,070
Stop signs used to be yellow.

2
00:00:02,750 --> 00:00:04,030
So why did they turn red?

3
00:00:04,530 --> 00:00:07,130
In 1923, American road engineers made a

4
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:09,380
rule: the more sides, the more danger.

5
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:11,200
A circle for railway crossings.

6
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:13,040
Eight sides for stop.

7
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:15,420
And for about thirty years, most stop

8
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:17,410
signs were yellow, with black letters.

9
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:18,710
Red would be better.

10
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:21,610
So why wait until 1954?

11
00:00:22,090 --> 00:00:24,350
Because red paint faded in the sun.

12
00:00:24,770 --> 00:00:26,630
And a pale pink stop sign is easy

13
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:27,190
to miss.
